  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Knowledge exchange at Agrofood Fair</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The horticulture sector in Ghana is an underdeveloped yet promising industry, with the potential to boost economic growth and youth employment.The Netherlands embassy in Accra, Ghana aims to bring systemic change and professionalism to this sector, focusing on open field farmers producing vegetables and fruits for the domestic market.This &apos;professionalisation&apos;, intended as formulated in the combination approach strategy, addresses Ghana&apos;s need for sustainable solutions in the sector, while reducing reliance on imported food and food related products.The purpose of Netherlands&apos; representation during the Ghana Agrofoodfair is:&#x2022;	to offer a platform that enables established Dutch companies, as well as Dutch businesses new to Ghana to present itself,&#x2022;	to scope business potential,&#x2022;	to consolidate existing as well as establish new economic ties between the Netherlands and Ghana, particularly in the horticultural and food sector.Participating in the Ghana Agrofood fair (Accra) is part of the broader combi-objective to improve access for Dutch business to the Ghanaian markets on the longer term, to highlight Dutch knowledge and expertise to the benefit of Ghanaian SMEs and consumers, and to ultimately contribute to job creation, food security and climate smart production through Dutch solutions.</narrative>
  </description>
